Lara sits by the fire on an outcrop in  Peru having just survived a nasty  mauling from two Jaguars you can assume  from context that she's hurt and her  best friend who sits less than six feet  away remarks on it but her face is stony  she hasn't spoken a word since the  attack she's frustrated annoyed having  her momentum halted irritated at the  roadblock she's angry and even her  compassionate nature can't break through  the wall of rage she's built up in her  clashes with Trinity Lara is looking to  get her hands on an artifact before they  do and is doing anything she can to  [ __ ] the organization when she's  asked by a skeptical local why it's so  important to her to keep the artifact  from Trinity she tells her that they are  dangerous it's the same reasoning she's  been using for her entire journey but  now it comes off as a hollow explanation  from a woman who has nothing left but  her thirst for vengeance having watched  the credits roll on Lara's last two  adventures it's hard not to feel both  fond and protective of her her drive is  admirable and her passion for  archaeology is unparalleled but it's  hard to ignore the emptiness under the  surface of her actions in the early  hours of shadow of the Tomb Raider Lara  frequently ignores her basic needs her  wounds and even the well-being of those  around her if they threatened to slow  her down she diverts queries about her  injuries with explanations of her  discoveries without missing a beat  constantly seeking the next step in her  investigation at this point  Lara is running on sheer resolve  a new study published in the Proceedings  of the National Academy of Sciences  journal suggests that meaning in one's  life may be healthier than happiness if  this is the case Lara is well on her way  to being the poster child she's clearly  not a happy person but having lost  almost everyone close to her it isn't  hard to imagine why that said she seems  to be losing grip on the meaning in her  life as well  in the first game Lara was a victim of  circumstance  a survivor in rise of the Tomb Raider  she was prepared an adventurer searching  for the final piece of the puzzle from  her father's last mission in shadow of  the Tomb Raider Lara is single-minded  reckless and lethal throughout the  previous game Lara showed a willingness  to put her mission aside if it meant  lives would be saved as she watches a  young boy fall from a building in her  latest mission as a result of a disaster  she may have put in motion it's clear  she's no longer concerned with how her  actions affect others when she escapes  the tsunami her companion Jonah insists  they stay behind to help the survivors  but Lara is steadfast to the point of  obstinate that her mission to stop  Trinity comes first  early on in the lengthy gameplay demo  Lara has a moment of hesitation before  removing a priceless and foreboding  dagger from a tomb what follows is one  of the few breaks in her resolve a  simple what have I done  her dogged pursuit of Trinity also  enables her to ignore what all these  missions and all this murder is doing to  her mental stability towards the end of  rise of the Tomb Raider the Christ from  Trinity soldiers change from the  assumption that they can take her out  easily two phrases like West stuck in  here with her Lara's reputation carries  through into shadow where enemies are  more panicked in her presence  Christ look at her sir her fighting  style has also changed significantly to  reflect the way she has shut out aspects  of her humanity and adopted an icy  resolve while still perfectly capable  with a gun Lara has adopted a dirtier  approach where she will hide in  vegetation walls or slather herself in  mud to strike without warning for new  attacks are brutal animalistic and  underhanded one such ability lets her  string an enemy up by hanging them from  a tree branch with a rope arrow after  killing two Trinity soldiers she wonders  aloud what they're so afraid of the what  she's referring to is a mysterious  violent tribe in the jungle but it's  hard to ignore the irony given it to her  arrows sticking out of their skulls  what are they so afraid of upon  encountering this tribe at the end of  the gameplay demo she shoots on sight  there's enough doubt to suggest they are  as dangerous as she assumes but her lack  of hesitation is a stark contrast to the  young woman who a year prior broke down  after wrestling a gun from an attacker  and shooting him to save herself  after she refuses to aid the injured  civilians Jonah yells at Lara telling  her that not everything is about her  this is directly after she faces the  leader of Trinity who accuses her of  unleashing a tragedy and realizes she  has done exactly as she feared her enemy  would have an understated comment that  stuck with me though is a description of  Lara uttered by a Trinity soldier in one  of the first scenes of the game you have  the photo  female Caucasian early 20s Lara is  admirable and intelligent and the turtle  badass but she's also incredibly young  and while her circumstances aren't  relatable her age is like anyone in  their early 20s it's not so much the  mistake she's making now and the things  that have happened to her but the way  she decides to respond going forward how  she reflects on herself and if she  repositioned her priorities that will  define the person she becomes in the  final chapter of her journey what will I  become
 

